> Error in if (empty(new)) return(data.frame()) :
>    missing value where TRUE/FALSE needed

An upper limit of 400 would be consistent with the idea that a break has
to appear in every facet:

 > ddply(ABC, .(t), summarise, range=t(range(z)))
   t range.1 range.2
1 1       1     400
2 2       2     800
3 3       3    1200
4 4       4    1600
5 5       5    2000
6 6       6    2400
7 7       7    2800
8 8       8    3200
9 9       9    3600

Which also would be why 0 didn't help; it wasn't in any range.  A few more:

 > ABC.g    + stat_contour(aes(x=x,y=y,z=z),breaks=c(8, 500, 1000))
 > ABC.g    + stat_contour(aes(x=x,y=y,z=z),breaks=c(8))

Error in if (empty(new)) return(data.frame()) :
   missing value where TRUE/FALSE needed

 > ABC.g    + stat_contour(aes(x=x,y=y,z=z),breaks=c(8, 3601))

Error in if (empty(new)) return(data.frame()) :
   missing value where TRUE/FALSE needed

So another phrasing of what will cause the error: If any facet does not
include within its range of contoured values any of the listed breaks,
the error will happen.  I, too, will leave it to someone else to figure
out how to fix it.  But hopefully this will narrow things down enough
(or at least give plenty of test/edge cases).

